   "id": "landing",
   "title": "The Persians land at Marathon",
   "time": "Early September 490 BC",
   "narrative": "Datis and Artaphernes bring the fleet down the Attic coast on the advice of the exiled tyrant Hippias and beach it on the bay of Marathon, about 27 kilometres from Athens. The plain is a good place to land: open ground for horses, a long shore for the ships. Under Miltiades the Athenian army marches out fast and takes the high ground at the plain's south-western edge, on a spur of Mount Agrieliki, blocking the exits toward Athens.",
