   "narrative": "The runner Pheidippides has gone to Sparta, but the Spartans cannot march before the full moon because of a religious festival. Athens must hold on. A full muster of 1,000 Plataean hoplites arrives, which steadies Athenian nerves. Ten generals share command, with the war archon Callimachus in overall charge. For about five days the armies sit facing each other across the plain: the Athenians gain by waiting for the Spartans, the Persians hesitate to attack hoplites head on.",
